{"_id":"68a736358ec3d8323af1db0a","nodeId":"b1iYy4Hvkj47Q13V2HE4i","roadmapSlug":"rust","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:32.844Z","description":"# Hashset\n\n`HashSet<T>` is a collection of unique elements using hash-based storage for fast lookups, insertions, and deletions. No duplicates are allowed and elements are unordered. Provides methods like `insert()`, `contains()`, and `remove()`. Example: `let mut set = HashSet::new(); set.insert(\"value\");`","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"HashSet in std::collections","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/collections/struct.HashSet.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfddad"},{"type":"official","title":"Hashset","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/std/hash/hashset.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfddae"},{"type":"video","title":"Rust HashSet Collection Type","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KYw3Lnf0nSY&t=1440s","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfddaf"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:07:02.070Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/rust/content/b1iYy4Hvkj47Q13V2HE4i.md"}